+++ b/DOCS/man/ao.rst
@@ -321,3 +321,29 @@ Available audio output drivers are:
         cases, but reportedly on some devices there are glitches following
         stream resets under the default setting. In such cases, specifying a
         shorter duration might help.
+
+``mediafoundation``
+    Dolby Digital Plus through the decoder Windows ships (Media Foundation).
+
+    Used for E-AC-3 that mpv passes through (``--audio-spdif=eac3``) to a
+    device that refuses the bitstream: ``wasapi`` hands the stream over to it,
+    together with the device it was opened for (the default one, or the one
+    selected with ``--audio-device=wasapi/...``). Instead of sending the
+    bitstream to the device, it hands the access units to the system's Dolby
+    decoder. With a spatial sound format active on the device (Dolby Atmos for
+    Headphones, for home theater, for built-in speakers) the decoder renders a
+    Dolby Atmos track as objects, which mpv's own decoder cannot do. It is not
+    probed on its own and has no entries in ``--audio-device=help``;
+    ``--ao=mediafoundation`` selects it directly.
+
+    The output refuses to initialize, and mpv decodes the track itself, when no
+    decoder on the system offers spatial objects for the device. If the stream
+    fails while playing, mpv decodes the rest of the track itself. When the
+    device changes (another default device, the device removed, a new device
+    format), the output is reopened, which tries passthrough again.
+
+    The following global options are supported by this audio output:
+
+    ``--ao-mediafoundation-require-spatial=<yes|no>``
+        Whether to refuse when the decoder would output plain PCM (default:
+        yes).
